{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1020824-about-frenzy","id":1020824,"title":"About frenzy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-22T04:48:33-08:00","id":1020824,"title":"About frenzy","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I need some clarification about frenzy.<br /> <br /> If a vampire fails the roll (resolve+composure) while facing a frenzy check she enters in frenzy, now, how can she exit frenzy?<br /> <br /> The book states:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A point of Willpower holds off the Beast for one turn. The vampire visibly fights the frenzy. She may growl, hiss, smash something, or sprint off. But she\u2019s temporarily in control. However, she must still face her Beast. Once she stops spending Willpower, make the Resolve + Composure roll like normal, but take a bonus die for each Willpower point spent. </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering if this means that, after falling into uncontrolled frenzy, a vampire could hold on the frenzy for each turns she spends a willpower than, at will, she can reroll resolve+composure + die bonuses equals to willpower spent?<br /> <br /> It sound weird to me and is too easy to ending frenzy in this way. Can you clarify me this mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T05:43:40-08:00","id":1020837,"title":"","content":"The quote you're mentioning only works before you've actually entered Frenzy. You can't do that once you've already entered it.<br /> <br /> The very next two paragraphs answer your question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Upon entering frenzy, determine what the Beast wants.<br /> Does it want to escape? Does it want to punish the person who<br /> insulted his host? Does it want blood? Typically, frenzy ends<br /> when that thing occurs. Some Devotions and Coils may end<br /> frenzy prematurely. If the character enters torpor, the frenzy ends.<br /> <br /> A vampire\u2019s Touchstone can talk her down from frenzy with<br /> an extended Social roll, requiring a number of successes equal<br /> to three times the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency. The Touchstone<br /> can make one roll per turn. So a Blood Potency 4 vampire\u2019s<br /> Touchstone would require 12 successes to talk her out of frenzy.<br /> During this time, the vampire\u2019s likely to cause significant<br /> problems for herself and others. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:27:53-08:00","id":1020870,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the clarification <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T04:50:30-08:00","id":1021528,"title":"","content":"So, if I fall in frenzy beacause someone provokes me, the Beast goal would be to kill him but he manages to escape and disappear. So, when the frenzy would end as it can't pursue its goal anymore? Should the beast change the goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T07:01:29-08:00","id":1021555,"title":"","content":"No hard rules, there, that's why the book says &quot;typically&quot;. If the Beast can reasonably think that the target is still reachable, it can try to hunt the target down. With vampiric senses, probably it is a fairly good guess. If the target eludes the Beast long enough, it can either subsume the Frenzy or change target to something it thinks to be responsible for the original target's escape.<br /> <br /> But, as I said, no fast rules. The ST is the only true judge for this, and the answer can be distinct every time. Just go for what's the best for the chronicle. More often than not, keeping a frenzy too long or purposeless is just boring, nut not always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:14:59-08:00","id":1021736,"title":"","content":"The frenzy would probably end either when the Beast decides it's no longer possible to achieve its goal or at the end of the scene. I think it requires the fifth dot of the Coil of the Wyrm to maintain a frenzy for longer than one scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}